; C and Z. BOTH transforms are printed by Tools/gen_nunchuk.gd — position and rake
; together — rather than authored here. Re-run it and paste; do not nudge these by eye.
;
; They used to share a hand-picked Rx(-55), on the reasoning that the shelf faces up
; and forward at 35 degrees. The front face is not a plane: its reach peaks around
; t = 0.16 and falls away either side, so C sits ABOVE that brow facing +13 degrees
; and Z sits BELOW it facing -18.4 degrees — 31 degrees apart, and Z a full 53 degrees
; from what it was given. On a 20 mm blade that error buried one end 9 mm inside the
; shell and stood the other 6 mm off it, which is why Z could be seen from underneath
; the nunchuk: the low end was sticking clean out through the belly.
[node name="CButton" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="." unique_id=1185203229]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.22519, -0.97431, 0, 0.97431, 0.22519, 0, 0.04011, -0.01616)
mesh = ExtResource("9_ncc")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_key")

[node name="ZButton" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="." unique_id=204491322]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, -0.31521, -0.94902, 0, 0.94902, -0.31521, 0, 0.02517, -0.01308)
